On 2004-08-03, Death Quaker <deathquaker@hotmail.com> wrote:
> So--finally, and thanks if you're still reading this--here's the
> question: what's a Wizard to do when she can't find non-metal armor? I
> was high enough level I was attracting monsters who hit well and hard;
> I really needed a decent AC.


First of all, try to have ways to escape- ways to teleport [even
uncontrolled], wands of digging, cursed potions of gain
level, etc can all get you away from a hazardous situation..

Second, with an athame, you can engrave Elbereth all that you want- which
significantly reduces the ways you can get attacked.. Another thing with the
same effect is standing on a scroll of scare monster.. if you pick up a
scroll and it crumbles to dust, it must be scare monster [iirc, cursed
scrolls always crumble, blessed scrolls become uncursed, and uncursed scrolls
that have been picked up once crumble]- if you cant write on the square you
are on for whatever reason, you can probably still drop one of these.

Third- magic missle is an excellent weapon- if you have a lot of monsters
around and are near some walls, think about how the spell will bounce- you
might be able to take out multiple monsters with one spell (as a side note,
if you are tricky enough, you can take out a unicorn with an appropriate
spell or wand if you can line up the bounce right). 

Fourth- I recommend going to the oracle level to look for spell books,
statues have a random chance of having spell books in them, and the oracle
level has many statues- depending on its depth, you could have a very good
chance of finding a few spells..  [see misc-343.txt.gz in the spoilers for
details]

